### 3.6 Global 403-on-suspended handling

`AuthContext.tsx` already wraps API calls indirectly via `useAuth()`. Add a small interceptor at the `apiClient` layer in `frontend/src/lib/api.ts` that does this on any 403:

```ts
if (response.status === 403) {
  const body = await response.clone().json().catch(() => null);
  if (body?.detail === "ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED") {
    // hard sign-out path
    window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent("tourwise:account-suspended", { detail: body }));
  }
  // still throw so the caller can react
  throw new Error(body?.detail || `HTTP ${response.status}`);
}
```

Then in `AuthContext.tsx`:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  const handler = () => {
    toast.error("Your account has been suspended by an admin.");
    void signOut();
    navigate("/login");
  };
  window.addEventListener("tourwise:account-suspended", handler);
  return () => window.removeEventListener("tourwise:account-suspended", handler);
}, [signOut, navigate]);
```

This keeps the matching logic out of every individual page.

