## Acceptance checklist

After Phase 3 lands, manually verify:

- [ ] `/admin/manage-users` → Travelers tab loads real users from `profiles`. Search by name/email returns hits.
- [ ] Ban a traveler for 24h → their next request returns 403 with `detail=ACCOUNT_SUSPENDED` → they're auto-signed-out and bounced to `/login` with a toast. Confirmed in the network tab via the browser dev console.
- [ ] Same banned traveler can sign up again with a *different* email; new account is active immediately.
- [ ] Wait 24h (or temporarily set duration to a few seconds in the DB) → ban auto-expires, user can log back in without an admin action.
- [ ] Permanent ban behaves the same but never expires (`banned_until = 'infinity'`).
- [ ] Admins cannot ban other admins (route returns 422 or 403).
- [ ] Agents tab → Active sub-list shows CNIC and current ban status; `total_trips` column is populated (no more empty cells).
- [ ] Ban an active agent → their account is locked AND `banned_cnics` has a row for their CNIC. Trying to register a new account with the same CNIC against `POST /api/register-as-agent` returns 403 with the ban reason.
- [ ] Unban the agent → both the profile lock and the `banned_cnics` row are reversed (`lifted_at` set); a fresh re-registration with the same CNIC succeeds.
- [ ] Existing flows (`/admin/dashboard`, `/admin/manage-agents` Pending tab, agent verification submission) still work unchanged.
- [ ] No new npm or pip dependencies introduced.

